# Review: DevtoolsPlugin

The devtools tree is solid. `createDevtoolsExtension` hangs the full Client/HALO/ECHO/MESH/Agent/EDGE tree, App
Graph, SDK Explorer and CLI off `root/debug`, `react-surface.ts` registers one `@dxos/devtools` article per node,
and `app-graph-builder.test.ts` checks the tree position and that pages have no URL. The Stats companion and
Agent › HALO are built as described. Most of the rest of the spec describes `@dxos/plugin-debug`, so those items
were judged against that package. There, several items are stale. `DebugStatus` shows error, swarm and saving
indicators, not a generator running state, and `DebugContextType` does not exist. Log download uses a browser
download, not the file uploader. `LoggingArticle` streams from the client's logging service and ignores
`logStore`. `GithubPanel` lists merged PRs and no surface registers it. No scenario or QA test has automation;
the only end-to-end coverage is the storage-version e2e test for F-8.

Of 43 items: 7 done, 19 untested, 1 partial, 7 diverged, 9 missing.

## Extensions

| Term      | URI                        |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| `verdict` | `org.dxos.mdl.verdict@1.0` |

